  ["forever.druid-balance.split"] = "whether to level it at all. Method calls Balance viable and best taken beyond 30, and Mobalytics uses it only as the tail of a Feral build. The first 11 points follow wow.gg's level 20 page, and the rest are ours from the row gates and Method's and Warcraft Tavern's named priorities. Nobody has written a full order.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.dry"] = "A monster that is hitting you is not hitting anyone else, and that is the whole job.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.intro"] = "Feral as a bear holds monsters while a group kills them. Bear Form comes at 10. Lacerate at 25 and Primal Bite at 40 make the threat, and Frenzied Regeneration and Barkskin keep you alive. It is the cat's tree with different points.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.line"] = "Bear Form from 10, Lacerate and Primal Bite for threat. It holds a pack for the group.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.note"] = "(43 points in Feral Combat, 8 in Restoration for Heart of the Wild and Natural Shapeshifter.)",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p1"] = "Maul, Swipe and Primal Bite cost less Rage, so you spend it on more attacks. Rage is the only thing a bear runs on.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p10"] = "Your party crits more often while you are in Bear Form. The group gets it for free, and Primal Bite at 40 needs it.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p11"] = "A critical strike gives you extra Rage. More Rage is more Maul and Swipe, so a crit helps your threat twice.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p12"] = "More armour in Bear Form. Armour stops part of every hit, and a tank takes the most hits. Method's dungeon tank takes it.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p13"] = "Your melee attacks do more to a bleeding monster. Lacerate keeps one bleeding, so Maul and Swipe gain from it on every pull.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p14"] = "A heavy bite that makes a lot of threat, on a short cooldown. Mobalytics calls it a must for tanking a pack.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p15"] = "You dodge more, and a dodge can give you Rage. A tank that is hit less needs less healing, and the Rage pays for Maul.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p16"] = "Shifting into Bear Form can give you Rage at once, so you open a pull with Rage to spend.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p17"] = "Your melee crits hurt more. Lacerate and Maul crit more with Sharpened Claws, so it adds threat.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p18"] = "More Stamina in Bear Form, which is more health to be hit with, and more Intellect for the heals between pulls.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p19"] = "Shifting costs less mana. You shift to heal between pulls and shift back, and each shift costs a large part of your mana.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p2"] = "Swipe hits harder. Swipe is your attack against two or three monsters, and most of your threat until Lacerate.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p3"] = "Bash stuns longer and comes back sooner. A stun that is ready more often is a monster that does nothing more often.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p4"] = "Maul and Swipe hit harder. It is also the gate to Lacerate at 25, so these two points have to come first.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p5"] = "In Bear Form it holds a monster and cuts off a spell. It gets you to the monster that is running at your healer.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p6"] = "You crit more often in Cat Form and Bear Form. It is also the gate to Blood Frenzy.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p7"] = "A bleed that stacks 5 times and makes a lot of threat. Mobalytics says to skip it unless you tank dungeons, and you do.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p8"] = "More attack power in Bear Form, scaled to your level, so your swings make more threat. It is the gate to Rend and Tear.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.p9"] = "A critical strike gives you extra Rage. More Rage is more Maul and Swipe, so a crit helps your threat twice.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build. Wrath and Moonfire from range do the killing, Healing Touch and Rejuvenation keep you up, and Bear Form and your first talent point come at 10.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.s1.between1.if"] = "after a fight, if you are hurt, from 4",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.s1.between1.why"] = "it heals while you drink",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.s1.between2.if"] = "when it has run out",
