  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.split"] = "Rend and Tear against Natural Reaction, and Lacerate. Method takes Rend and Tear for its dungeon tank, Mobalytics offers either, and Mobalytics skips Lacerate unless you tank. The points after 30 are ours from the row gates, and nobody has played past 30.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-bear.variant"] = "bear",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.dry"] = "Shred wants you behind the monster. Claw does not mind where you stand.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.intro"] = "Feral as a cat kills one monster at a time with Energy and combo points: Rake and Rip bleed, Claw and Shred build, Ferocious Bite finishes. Cat Form comes at 20, so levels 10 to 19 are spent in Bear Form with the same points. Guides level Feral over every other spec on Forever.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.line"] = "Cat Form from 20, bleeds and a finisher. A bear until then, and the one every guide levels.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.note"] = "(31 points in Feral Combat, 7 in Balance for Genesis and Nature's Majesty, 13 in Restoration for Heart of the Wild, Naturalist and Natural Shapeshifter.)",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p1"] = "Maul, Swipe, Claw and Rake cost less Rage or Energy. You are a bear until 20, so it helps from the first fight, and Mobalytics and Method both put it first.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p10"] = "Your party crits more often while you are in Cat Form. Method and Mobalytics both take it at 30.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p11"] = "Your melee crits hurt more. Mobalytics takes it straight after Leader of the Pack.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p12"] = "Shred costs less Energy again, so you land it more often. Method and Maxroll open from behind and Shred.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p13"] = "Your melee attacks do more to a bleeding monster. Rake and Rip keep one bleeding, so most of your fight is spent in this bonus.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p14"] = "Turns mana into Energy on a cooldown. Method uses it when Energy runs low. Mobalytics skips it, so this is a split, and it costs mana.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p15"] = "Bleeds and heals over time do a little more with each rank. Rake and Rip are both over time. Mobalytics starts its tail here.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p16"] = "A little more crit chance with spells and melee attacks. Mobalytics pairs it with Nature's Reach, which only helps spells, so the build stops at two ranks.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p17"] = "More Intellect, more Stamina in Bear Form and more Strength in Cat Form. It is the gate to Naturalist.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p18"] = "All the damage you deal rises with each rank. Mobalytics takes it last, after Heart of the Wild.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p19"] = "Shifting costs less mana, Shifting Power included. A cat that turns bear for a pack shifts a lot.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p2"] = "Swipe hits harder, and monsters notice you less while you Prowl. Swipe is your attack against a pack, and you are a bear until 20.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p3"] = "More movement speed in Cat Form and a better chance to dodge. Taking it now means it is full when Cat Form comes at 20.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p4"] = "You crit more often in Cat Form and Bear Form, so every attack you make gains from it.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p5"] = "In Cat Form it leaps you behind the monster, so Shred works after it. In Bear Form it holds the monster and cuts off a spell.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p6"] = "Claw, Rake, Shred, Maul and Swipe hit harder. These are the attacks you use all fight.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p7"] = "More attack power in Cat Form and Bear Form, scaled to your level. It is also the gate to Rend and Tear.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p8"] = "It changes how Ferocious Bite spends spare Energy, and it is the gate to Shifting Power at 40.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.p9"] = "Shred costs less Energy. Shred is your hardest hit while you are behind the monster, so it earns each rank when you can get there.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build. Wrath and Moonfire from range do the killing, Healing Touch and Rejuvenation keep you up, and Bear Form and your first talent point come at 10.",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.between1.if"] = "after a fight, if you are hurt, from 4",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.between1.why"] = "it heals while you drink",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.between2.if"] = "when it has run out",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.between2.why"] = "armour for an hour is cheap",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.between3.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.between3.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.between3.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.loop1.if"] = "when your health is low",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.loop1.why"] = "a heal costs less than a death",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.loop2.if"] = "on a monster that will live a while",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.loop2.why"] = "it keeps hurting it while you cast Wrath",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.loop3.if"] = "while you have mana",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.loop3.why"] = "it is your main attack",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.loop4.why"] = "a swing costs no mana, so use it when the mana is gone",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.low1.if"] = "when your mana is nearly gone",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.low1.why"] = "a swing costs no mana",
  ["forever.druid-feral-cat.s1.low2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
