  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.between4.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.between4.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.big"] = "Innervate when your mana runs low, Nature's Swiftness when someone is about to die",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.loop1.if"] = "when a target with your heal on it is dropping",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.loop1.why"] = "it heals at once, from the heal already there",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.loop2.if"] = "when several in the party are hurt",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.loop2.why"] = "it heals the target and the whole party",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.loop3.if"] = "when the tank is falling behind",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.loop3.why"] = "it heals now and keeps healing",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.loop4.if"] = "for a big hit",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.loop4.why"] = "it is the biggest heal you have",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.loop5.why"] = "it is the cheapest heal you have, so keep it on the tank",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.low1.if"] = "when your mana is nearly gone",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.low1.text"] = "Heal only the tank",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.low1.why"] = "one heal that lands beats three you cannot afford",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.low2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.low2.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.low2.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.opening1.if"] = "before the first pull",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.opening1.why"] = "it raises your armour for an hour",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.opening2.if"] = "on the tank, before each pull",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.opening2.why"] = "it hurts every monster that hits them",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.opening3.if"] = "on the tank, before the pull",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.opening3.why"] = "it heals before the first hit lands",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.opening4.if"] = "on the tank, if the pull is hard",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.opening4.why"] = "it heals now and keeps healing",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.rarely1.if"] = "when the whole party is hurt",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.rarely1.why"] = "it heals all of them over a few seconds",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.rarely2.if"] = "to bring back a dead player in a fight",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.rarely2.why"] = "it raises them at once, with a long wait after",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.rarely3.if"] = "when a poison is on someone",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.rarely3.why"] = "it cures a poison, and another every few seconds",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.rarely4.if"] = "before the first pull, from 50",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.s4.rarely4.why"] = "it buffs the whole party at once",
  ["forever.druid-restoration.split"] = "whether to level in it at all. Warcraft Tavern says not to, Method gives it no build and Maxroll writes a healer's page for dungeons. The first 13 points follow wow.gg's healing page and Mobalytics' Reflection, and the order after that is ours from the row gates. Nobody has played past 30.",
  ["forever.druid.advice.damage"] = "Feral as a cat is the damage build this page advises, because guides level Feral over every other spec and you fight as a bear until Cat Form at 20 with the same points. The price: a cat cannot cast or heal in form. Balance casts from range and levels slowly alone.",
  ["forever.druid.advice.heal"] = "Restoration is the healer. Guides do not level it alone, so level as Feral and respec for dungeons. The price: a respec costs gold, and Restoration kills slowly by itself.",
  ["forever.druid.advice.tank"] = "Feral as a bear is the tank. Bear Form comes at 10, Lacerate at 25 and Primal Bite at 40 for threat. The price: it is the cat's tree, so the points that tank and the points that kill are not the same, and a respec between them costs gold.",
  ["forever.druid.ov.bad"] = "Staying in one place. Every shift costs mana, you cannot cast or heal in a form, and the caster specs are slow alone.",
  ["forever.druid.ov.good"] = "Doing the job in front of you. A Druid levels well as a bear or a cat, heals a group between pulls and brings a dead player back with Rebirth.",
  ["forever.druid.ov.levelling"] = "Bear Form from 10 and Cat Form from 20. Until 20 you fight as a bear with Maul and Swipe. After that a cat takes single monsters and a bear takes packs, with a heal and a drink between fights. Check your form before each pull.",
  ["forever.druid.ov.resource"] = "Mana to shift and to cast, Rage in Bear Form, and Energy and combo points in Cat Form. Entering a form takes a large part of your mana, so drink before you shift back.",
  ["forever.druid.ov.ten"] = "You get your first talent point and Bear Form. Pick the spec: Feral levels fastest and is a cat or a bear, Balance casts from range and Restoration heals. A respec costs gold.",
  ["forever.druid.ov.who"] = "You are three classes in one and you choose which at the pull. With no form on you cast, in Bear Form you tank, in Cat Form you stab. A form costs mana to enter and then runs on Rage or Energy.",
  ["forever.druid.role.damage"] = "Guides level Feral over every other spec. You are a bear until Cat Form at 20, with the same points. Balance is the caster and slower alone.",
  ["forever.druid.role.heal"] = "The only healing build. Guides do not level it alone, so level as Feral and respec for dungeons.",
  ["forever.druid.role.tank"] = "The only tanking build. Bear Form comes at 10, Lacerate at 25 and Primal Bite at 40 for threat.",
  ["forever.hunter"] = "A bow or a gun, a pet, and a lot of distance. Auto Shot, Raptor Strike and Track Beasts are yours from the start, Serpent Sting and Aspect of the Monkey come at 4, Hunter's Mark and Arcane Shot at 6. At 10 a class quest gives you a pet, and Aspect of the Hawk comes with it. Every line below says where to stand, what to shoot and when to send the pet.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.dry"] = "A dead pet leaves you alone with the monster, so keep it mended.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.intro"] = "Beast Mastery makes the pet the other half of your damage. Deadly Aspects speeds your shots, Summon Hawk lets two hawks fight beside your pet from 25, and Bestial Wrath makes the pet hit much harder at 40. It is the easiest Hunter to level.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.line"] = "Your pet and two hawks do much of the work. The easiest Hunter to level, and the pet carries the pulls.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.note"] = "(31 points in Beast Mastery, then 20 in Marksmanship for critical hits and Mortal Shots.)",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p1"] = "With Aspect of the Hawk on, Auto Shot sometimes speeds up your shooting by 30% for 12 seconds. The full orders start here.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p10"] = "Your pet stuns the monster for 3 seconds on its next hit, and that hit crits far more often. It is the way to Bestial Wrath.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p11"] = "Ferocity is full, which opens Frenzy.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p12"] = "Doubles your pet's Focus regeneration and lets half your mana regeneration go on while you cast. Kargoz takes it here, Vareion at 38.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p13"] = "After a critical hit your pet sometimes attacks 30% faster for 8 seconds. Kargoz stops at four points, Vareion takes five.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p14"] = "You and your pet regain 1% of your health every 5 seconds while the pet is out. Kargoz takes one point, Vareion none.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p15"] = "Your pet deals 50% more damage for 18 seconds. It is the end of the tree, and every point before it was spent to reach it.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p16"] = "1% more critical strike chance on all your attacks. The Marksmanship points start here in both full orders.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p17"] = "6 yards more range on your ranged weapons. More range is more time before the monster reaches you.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p18"] = "Your attack power rises by your Intellect, so gear with Intellect pays twice, in mana and in damage.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p19"] = "Rapid Fire comes back 2 minutes sooner, and a kill under your Serpent Sting makes your next shot hit 20% harder.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p2"] = "2% more damage for you and your pet while the pet is out. It is the one talent on this row that adds damage.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p20"] = "Critical hits with ranged abilities deal 30% more. It needs Careful Aim, so it comes last.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p3"] = "Revive Pet casts 6 seconds faster and costs 40% less mana. These two points help reach the ten that row 2 asks for. Pathfinding cannot come before ten points.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p4"] = "15% more health and armour for your pet. This point is the tenth, which opens row 2, and a tougher pet holds a pull longer.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p5"] = "Your pet moves 30% faster. Intimidation needs it, and Bestial Wrath needs Intimidation.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p6"] = "Your pets and hawks deal up to 20% more damage, and the hawks of Summon Hawk count. Kargoz and Vareion both take all five.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p7"] = "A hawk dives at the monster, hits at once and keeps attacking for 18 seconds. Two hawks can be out together. Kargoz calls it a huge power spike.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p8"] = "Your pets and hawks deal the full 20% more damage once this point is in.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.p9"] = "Your pet and hawks crit up to 16% more often. Frenzy needs all five points, so these come first.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1"] = "Before your first talent point and before your pet. The same kit in every build. Pull from as far as you can reach and back away from what gets close.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.between1.if"] = "before you leave town",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.between1.text"] = "Check your ammunition",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.between1.why"] = "Auto Shot and Volley need it",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.between2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.between2.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.between2.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.loop1.if"] = "whenever it is ready",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.loop1.why"] = "it is instant, so you can step back after it",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.loop2.if"] = "when the monster gets close",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.loop2.why"] = "it slows the monster so you can back away",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.loop3.if"] = "when it reaches you",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.loop3.why"] = "it hits hard in melee",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.loop4.why"] = "it costs no mana",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.low1.if"] = "when your mana is nearly gone",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.low1.why"] = "it costs no mana",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.opening1.if"] = "before the first pull",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.opening1.why"] = "it raises your chance to dodge",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.opening2.if"] = "on a monster that will live a while",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.opening2.why"] = "your shots gain ranged attack power against it",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.opening3.if"] = "from as far away as it reaches",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.opening3.say"] = "stand still so it fires",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.opening3.why"] = "the pull is free and the monster walks to you",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.opening4.if"] = "on a monster that will live a while",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s1.opening4.why"] = "it burns while you shoot",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2"] = "Your pet quest is at 10: tame a boar, call it out and keep it fed. Mark the monster, send the pet in and shoot from range. Aspect of the Hawk replaces the Monkey once a pet holds the monster.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between1.if"] = "once the class quest teaches it",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between1.why"] = "a boar holds threat, takes hits and eats anything",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between2.if"] = "after a fight, if the pet is hurt",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between2.why"] = "it heals your pet while you focus",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between3.if"] = "when your pet is unhappy",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between3.why"] = "feeding it raises its happiness",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between4.if"] = "if your pet is not out",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between4.why"] = "it holds the monster while you shoot",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between5.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between5.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between5.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between6.if"] = "when you learn a new rank",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.between6.why"] = "your pet learns it from you",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.loop1.if"] = "whenever it is ready",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.loop1.why"] = "it is instant, so you can step back after it",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.loop2.if"] = "against two or more monsters",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.loop2.why"] = "it hits up to three",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.loop3.if"] = "right after you dodge",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.loop3.why"] = "it only works after a dodge",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.loop4.if"] = "when it reaches you",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.loop4.why"] = "it hits hard in melee",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.loop5.why"] = "it costs no mana",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.low1.if"] = "when your mana is nearly gone",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.low1.why"] = "it costs no mana",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.opening1.if"] = "if it is not on",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.opening1.why"] = "it adds attack power to every shot",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.opening2.if"] = "on a monster that will live a while",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.opening2.why"] = "your shots gain ranged attack power against it",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.opening3.if"] = "as soon as the monster is marked",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.opening3.text"] = "Send your pet in",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.opening3.why"] = "it takes the first hits",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.opening4.if"] = "on a single monster that will live a while",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.opening4.why"] = "it burns while you shoot",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.rarely1.if"] = "if a monster runs at you",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.rarely1.why"] = "it slows the monster so you can back away",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.rarely2.if"] = "when the monster is on you",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.rarely2.why"] = "it slows the monster so you can step away",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.rarely3.if"] = "when your pet has died",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s2.rarely3.why"] = "it comes back with a little health",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3"] = "Aimed Shot and Freezing Trap come at 20, Rapid Fire at 26, Feign Death at 30. Summon Hawk at 25 changes the pull: the hawks hit while your pet holds the monster. Intimidation at 30 stuns what the pet hits.",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between1.if"] = "after a fight, if the pet is hurt",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between1.why"] = "it heals your pet while you focus",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between2.if"] = "when your pet is unhappy",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between2.why"] = "feeding it raises its happiness",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between3.if"] = "if your pet is not out",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between3.why"] = "it holds the monster while you shoot",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between4.if"] = "to travel, out of a fight",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between4.why"] = "it is faster than walking, and a hit dazes you",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between5.if"] = "when you learn a new rank",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between5.why"] = "your pet learns it from you",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between6.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between6.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.between6.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.big"] = "on a hard pull or an elite, it makes you shoot much faster",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.loop1.if"] = "whenever it is ready",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.loop1.why"] = "two hawks can bite at once",
  ["forever.hunter-beast-mastery.s3.loop2.if"] = "when two hawks are already out",
