  ["forever.mage-frost.split"] = "the first points and the tail. Mobalytics takes Improved Frostbolt first, Conquest Capped would take Precision first for monsters above your level, and Icy Veins opens in Arcane for Missile Barrage. After 40 Mobalytics goes to Arcane for mana, Conquest Capped to Fire. The Arcane tail is Mobalytics'.",
  ["forever.mage.advice.damage"] = "Frost is the build this page advises, because it keeps monsters off you. Arcane is the other road guides name, and Method says it out-damages Frost when you quest alone.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.bad"] = "Being hit. You have little health and a cast that is interrupted is a turn lost. Two monsters at once is the usual way a mage dies.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.good"] = "Damage at range, and keeping monsters away with slows, freezes and a sheep. You make your own food and water, and you can carry a group's.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.levelling"] = "Frostbolt from as far as you can reach, Frost Nova when it gets close, step back and cast again. Drink between pulls. Pull one monster at a time until you are sure.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.resource"] = "Mana, and it is the whole game. Every cast spends it, so you cast, wait and drink. The wand costs none, and you must stand still to use it.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.ten"] = "You get your first talent point. Pick a build and Primer shows your first picks. Frost is the safest way to level alone, and a respec costs gold.",
  ["forever.mage.ov.who"] = "You hurt things from a distance with a cast bar and a mana bar. The craft is what to cast and when to stand still, and a monster that reaches you has won a round.",
  ["forever.mage.role.damage"] = "Most guides level Frost. It slows and freezes what reaches you, and Ice Lance on a frozen monster hits hardest.",
  ["forever.paladin"] = "Plate, mana and a seal. Seal of Righteousness, Holy Light and Devotion Aura are yours from the start, Judgement comes at 4, Holy Strike at 6. At 10 you get Seal of Fury, Righteous Fury and your first talent point. Every line below says what to have on you before it says what to press.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.dry"] = "A heal on a full bar is mana you do not have for the next one.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.intro"] = "Holy keeps people alive. It kills slowly alone, and a dungeon wants it. Holy Shock is both halves of the build, a heal on a friend and damage on an enemy, and Oath of Light and Light's Vigil are for the tank and the party.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.line"] = "Heals the group. It levels slowly alone, and a dungeon wants it.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.note"] = "(33 points in Holy, 13 in Retribution for Benediction, Conviction, Sanctified Judgement and Pursuit of Justice, 5 in Protection for Divine Intellect.)",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p1"] = "Your Flash of Light, Holy Light and Light's Vigil sometimes keep casting when you are hit. A healer casts under hits all day.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p10"] = "Holy Shock crits more often on a friend who does not carry your Oath of Light. Heal the tank with Holy Light and everyone else with Holy Shock.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p11"] = "Your Holy spells hit more often, and silences on you end sooner. Holy Shock and Exorcism should not miss.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p12"] = "Consecration, Exorcism, Holy Wrath and Hammer of Wrath cost less. They are the spells you kill with between heals.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p13"] = "Your critical heals heal even more. With Divine Favor and Illumination it is the most the tree gives a healer who crits.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p14"] = "Mark one friend, and your next Holy Shock on them has no cooldown and heals them and their party. It costs a lot, so use it when four or more are hurt.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p15"] = "Instant spells and abilities cost less. Holy Shock, Judgement and Holy Strike are instant, so you drink less.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p16"] = "Your heals and attacks crit more often, which feeds Illumination.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p17"] = "More Intellect, which is more mana, and a healer is limited by mana.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p18"] = "Judgement sometimes gives back part of the seal's mana, so you drink less. More points make it likelier.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p19"] = "You run and ride faster. Between pulls it saves more time than any other talent here, and guides call it the best stat for questing.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p2"] = "Part of your mana regeneration continues while you cast, and a healer casts all the time. It also opens Illumination.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p20"] = "Consecration, Exorcism, Holy Wrath and Hammer of Wrath cost less. They are the spells you kill with between heals.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p21"] = "Judgement sometimes gives back part of the seal's mana, so you drink less. More points make it likelier.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p22"] = "Cleanse and Purify cost less mana, and Exorcism and Holy Wrath come back sooner.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p3"] = "Holy Light, Flash of Light and Holy Shock heal more. It is the plain healing talent, and every heal you cast is bigger for it.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p4"] = "A critical heal sometimes gives back mana. The more you heal, the less you drink. It needs 2 points in Reverence.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p5"] = "Swear it on the tank: your Holy Light, Flash of Light and Holy Shock heal that target more. It is the one-target healer's talent.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p6"] = "Your next Flash of Light, Holy Light or Holy Shock is sure to crit. With Illumination, a big heal on it can pay its own mana back.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p7"] = "A critical Holy Shock or Flash of Light makes your next Holy Light cast faster.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p8"] = "Your Holy spells hit more often, and silences on you end sooner. Holy Shock and Exorcism should not miss.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.p9"] = "An instant heal on a friend, or Holy damage on an enemy. It is your quick heal and your way to kill alone, and it opens the last two talents.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build. A seal does most of your damage, and Judgement does not use it up, so use both.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.between1.if"] = "after a fight, if you are hurt",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.between1.why"] = "the cast is slow, so wait until nothing hits you",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.between2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.between2.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.between2.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.big"] = "keep it for the fight that would kill you",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.loop1.if"] = "when your health is low",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.loop1.why"] = "a heal costs less than a death",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.loop2.if"] = "whenever it is ready, from 4",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.loop2.why"] = "it hits hard and leaves the seal on you",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.loop3.if"] = "whenever it is ready, from 6",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.loop3.why"] = "it is a weapon strike with Holy damage added",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.loop4.if"] = "when it has ended",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.loop4.why"] = "swings add nothing without it",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.loop5.why"] = "swings are the rest of your damage",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.low1.if"] = "when your mana is nearly gone",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.low1.text"] = "Keep swinging",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.low1.why"] = "a swing costs no mana",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.low2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.low2.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.low2.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.opening1.if"] = "once, before anything",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.opening1.why"] = "it raises your armour until you change it",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.opening2.if"] = "before the first pull, from 4",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.opening2.why"] = "it adds attack power and lasts a long time",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.opening3.if"] = "just before the pull",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.opening3.why"] = "each swing adds Holy damage",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.rarely1.if"] = "if the monster runs, or you must heal",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s1.rarely1.why"] = "a stunned monster hits nothing",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s2"] = "Holy kills slowly alone and is made for a group. Judgement and Holy Strike are still most of your damage here, and the healing talents help your Holy Light. In a group, bless and heal.",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s2.alt.between1.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s2.alt.between1.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s2.alt.between1.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s2.alt.loop1.if"] = "when a friend is poisoned or diseased",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s2.alt.loop1.why"] = "it costs less than healing through it",
  ["forever.paladin-holy.s2.alt.loop2.if"] = "on whoever is hurt worst",
