  ["forever.paladin-protection.split"] = "when to go back to Protection. Icy Veins takes Retribution first, then Protection with little room to choose, and has no Toughness, Sacred Duty, Shield Specialization or Iron Creed. Mobalytics' final build, used here, has all four. Anticipation can move to Toughness or Guardian's Favor.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.dry"] = "Most of this page waits on Judgement. If it is not ready, hit the monster.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.intro"] = "Retribution fights in melee with one big weapon and a seal that adds to every swing. It is the Paladin that kills alone. Judgement no longer uses the seal up, and Holy Strike is a second button, so the page is about which seal and when to change it.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.line"] = "One big weapon, a seal, Judgement and Holy Strike. It kills alone, and every guide levels here.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.note"] = "(38 points in Retribution, 5 in Protection for Divine Intellect and 8 in Holy for Divine Strength and Improved Seals.)",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p1"] = "More parry, so fewer hits land, and a parry brings your next swing sooner. It is your safety while you learn what a pull costs.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p10"] = "A humanoid stops until something hurts it. Use it on the second monster of a pull, or on a runner while you heal. It also leads to the capstone.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p11"] = "A critical strike raises your Physical and Holy damage for a few seconds, and it stacks. It needs the Seal of Command talent.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p12"] = "Some of your hits lower the monster's attack power for a while, so its blows hurt less and you heal less.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p13"] = "Part of your Intellect becomes spell damage, so your Holy spells hit harder with Intellect on your gear. It opens the row of the capstone.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p14"] = "Your swings store a copy of your seal, and changing seal spends the copies. It is why a long fight swaps seals.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p15"] = "Instant spells and abilities cost less. Seals, Judgement and Holy Strike are all instant, so you drink less.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p16"] = "Part of your Intellect becomes spell damage, so your Holy spells hit harder with Intellect on your gear.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p17"] = "More Intellect, which is more mana. With Champion of the Light it is also more Holy damage.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p18"] = "More Strength, which is more attack power on every swing. It leads to Improved Seals.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p19"] = "Your seals and Judgements deal more damage. It is the Holy tree's damage talent for a melee Paladin.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p2"] = "Your spells and attacks crit more often. That includes the Holy damage on every swing.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p3"] = "Judgement comes back sooner. Most of your damage waits on it, so a shorter wait is more damage.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p4"] = "A swing sometimes adds Holy damage, and its Judgement hits a stunned monster harder. Take it with a slow weapon. With a fast one, keep Seal of Righteousness.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p5"] = "You run and ride faster. Between pulls it saves more time than any other talent here, and guides call it the best stat for questing.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p6"] = "Judgement sometimes gives back part of the seal's mana, so you drink less. More points make it likelier.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p7"] = "Holy Strike hits harder and refreshes the Judgement on its target. It keeps your Judgement up through a long fight.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p8"] = "Judgement sometimes gives back part of the seal's mana, so you drink less. More points make it likelier.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.p9"] = "Physical and Holy damage go up while you hold a two-hander, and the threat you make goes down. Alone, threat is not your problem.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build. A seal does most of your damage, and Judgement does not use it up, so use both.",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1.between1.if"] = "after a fight, if you are hurt",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1.between1.why"] = "the cast is slow, so wait until nothing hits you",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1.between2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1.between2.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1.between2.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1.big"] = "keep it for the fight that would kill you",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1.loop1.if"] = "when your health is low",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1.loop1.why"] = "a heal costs less than a death",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1.loop2.if"] = "whenever it is ready, from 4",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s1.loop2.why"] = "it hits hard and leaves the seal on you",
