  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.low2.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.opening1.if"] = "once, before anything",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.opening1.why"] = "a monster that hits you is hurt for it",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.opening2.if"] = "before the first pull",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.opening2.why"] = "it adds attack power and lasts a long time",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.opening3.if"] = "before the pull, slow weapon",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.opening3.why"] = "a slow weapon makes it hit hard",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.opening4.if"] = "before the pull, fast weapon",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.opening4.why"] = "a fast weapon makes it hit often",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.opening5.if"] = "as soon as the monster is in range",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.opening5.why"] = "it hits at once and leaves the seal on you",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.rarely1.if"] = "for a pack, not Holy Strike",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.rarely1.why"] = "it shares Holy Strike's cooldown, so pick one",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.rarely2.if"] = "on an Undead or a Demon",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.rarely2.why"] = "it only works on them, and it hits hard",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.rarely3.if"] = "if the monster runs, or you must heal",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.rarely3.why"] = "a stunned monster hits nothing",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.rarely4.if"] = "on a second humanoid",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.s4.rarely4.why"] = "it sleeps until something hurts it",
  ["forever.paladin-retribution.split"] = "the first points. Deflection first, as Mobalytics' two pages have it, or Benediction first, as Method and Icy Veins have it, for mana. The last 13 points are ours: guides stop at 30 and name Divine Strength, Improved Seals, Holy Conduit and Divine Intellect for the end.",
  ["forever.paladin.advice.damage"] = "Retribution is the build this page advises, because guides call it the Paladin to level alone and a seal does most of the work. The price: no taunt worth the name and no healing in a fight, so a dungeon wants a tank and a healer beside you.",
  ["forever.paladin.advice.heal"] = "Holy is the healer. Guides send you through Retribution to level and into Holy for dungeons, and this page puts the healing points first. The price: Holy kills slowly alone, so levelling takes longer.",
  ["forever.paladin.advice.tank"] = "Protection is the tank. Guides level it through Retribution up to 40, and this page spends its first 12 points there. The price: Holy Shield only comes at 42, and the spec is slow to quest alone.",
  ["forever.paladin.ov.bad"] = "Speed and crowds. You kill one monster at a time and wait for mana between pulls, and until Consecration there is nothing for a pack.",
  ["forever.paladin.ov.good"] = "Staying alive while you hit things. A group wants your auras and blessings, and you can always heal yourself when the fight is over.",
  ["forever.paladin.ov.levelling"] = "Seal on, Judgement when it is ready, Holy Strike when it is ready, swing the rest of the time. Heal when the fight is over and drink when the bar is low. Aura and blessing go on before the first pull.",
  ["forever.paladin.ov.resource"] = "Mana. Seals, Judgement, Holy Strike and heals spend it, and a swing costs none. When the bar is empty, keep swinging and sit down afterwards.",
  ["forever.paladin.ov.ten"] = "You get your first talent point and pick a spec. Retribution levels alone, Protection holds monsters for a group and Holy heals one. Most guides put the first points in Retribution, and the Holy page here does not. A respec costs gold.",
  ["forever.paladin.ov.who"] = "You fight in melee with a seal on you and heal yourself between pulls. It is slow work and hard to kill, and it runs on mana, not rage.",
  ["forever.paladin.role.damage"] = "Guides call Retribution the Paladin to level alone. A seal and Judgement do most of the work.",
  ["forever.paladin.role.heal"] = "The only healing build. It kills slowly alone and is made for a group, so level in Retribution first if you like.",
  ["forever.paladin.role.tank"] = "The only tanking build. Seal of Fury makes Judgement a taunt, and Consecration holds a pack.",
  ["forever.priest"] = "Cloth, mana and a wand. Smite and Lesser Heal are yours from the start, Shadow Word: Pain comes at 4, Power Word: Shield at 6, Renew and Fade at 8. At 10 you get Mind Blast and your first talent point. Every line below says what to put on first, what to cast and when to let the wand work.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.dry"] = "A shield on the tank is a hit you do not have to heal.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.intro"] = "Discipline levels like Shadow, with Pain, Mind Blast and the wand, and keeps a shield in reserve. Penance at 35, then Renewed Hope and Divine Aegis, make it a tank healer. Guides disagree on how fast it levels alone and agree that it heals well.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.line"] = "Shields, Penance and a wand. Levels like Shadow, and heals a tank.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.note"] = "(31 points in Discipline, 15 in Holy for Holy Specialization, Twilight Focus and Inspiration, 5 in Shadow for Spirit Tap.)",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p1"] = "Your wand does 25% more damage. It costs no mana, so most early kills end with it.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p10"] = "A volley that hurts an enemy or heals an ally, three times in 2 seconds. Cast it whenever it is ready, on a tank or on a monster.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p11"] = "Your single-target heals crit more on a target wearing Weakened Soul, and shorten it. Shield the tank, then heal into the shield.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p12"] = "A critical heal puts a shield on the target for 12 seconds. Renewed Hope makes your crits more common, so it fires often.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p13"] = "Your single-target heals crit more on a target wearing Weakened Soul, and shorten it. Shield the tank, then heal into the shield.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p14"] = "Smite, Holy Fire and instant spells cost 10% less. Shield and Renew are instant, so your healing costs less too.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p15"] = "Raises a target's spell damage and healing by 20% for 15 seconds. Cast it on a caster, or on yourself before a hard stretch.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p16"] = "Your Holy spells crit more often. It is a gate to the lower Holy talents, and Penance, Renewed Hope and your heals all use it.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p17"] = "Your spells keep their cast time when you are hit, most of the time. Pushback ends more heals than any monster does.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p18"] = "Renew heals more. It is the heal you put on the tank before the pull, so it gains from every rank you add.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p19"] = "Hurts every monster within 10 yards and heals your party. It is the only area damage spell you have, and it is in Holy.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p2"] = "Kills sometimes double your Spirit for 15 seconds, and half your mana regeneration continues while you cast for that time. It is why you drink so little.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p20"] = "A critical heal raises the target's armour for 15 seconds. Renewed Hope makes your crits more common, so the tank is often harder to hit.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p21"] = "Renew heals more. It is the heal you put on the tank before the pull, so it gains from every rank you add.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p3"] = "Your instant spells deal and heal more. Renew, Pain and Plague are instant, so it helps both halves of the build.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p4"] = "More Intellect, which is more mana and a little more critical chance.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p5"] = "Half your mana regeneration keeps going while you cast. A healer casts all the time, so this is the mana talent that matters most.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p6"] = "Your next spell costs nothing and crits more often. Put it on Greater Heal or Prayer of Healing when the big hit comes.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p7"] = "Your Power Word: Shield absorbs 20% more. The shield is the first thing you cast on the tank, so this works on every pull.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p8"] = "Power Word: Shield costs 15% less and comes back 4 seconds sooner. A shield you can recast often is the point of this tree.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.p9"] = "Smite, Holy Fire and instant spells cost less. Shield and Renew are instant, so your healing costs less too.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build. Get a wand as soon as you can, because from 5 it does most of your killing.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.between1.if"] = "after a fight, if you are hurt",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.between1.why"] = "it heals while you drink",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.between2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.between2.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.between2.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.loop1.if"] = "when your health is low",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.loop1.why"] = "a heal costs less than a death",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.loop2.if"] = "on a monster that will live a while",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.loop2.why"] = "it keeps hurting it while you wand",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.loop3.if"] = "until you have a wand",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.loop3.why"] = "it is the attack you start with",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.loop4.why"] = "the wand costs no mana, and it is not interrupted by hits",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.low1.if"] = "when your mana is nearly gone",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.low1.why"] = "it costs no mana and does not stop regeneration",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.opening1.if"] = "before the first pull",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.opening1.why"] = "a little more health for the whole fight",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.opening2.if"] = "before each pull, from 6",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.opening2.why"] = "it soaks a hit and damage cannot stop your cast",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.opening3.if"] = "from as far away as it reaches",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s1.opening3.why"] = "the monster spends its walk taking damage",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2"] = "Alone you level as a wand Priest: shield, Mind Blast, Pain and the wand. In a group, shield and Renew the tank and heal the rest. Penance does not come until 35.",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.between1.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.between1.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.between1.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.loop1.if"] = "when a friend has a harmful spell",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.loop1.why"] = "it costs less than healing through it",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.loop2.if"] = "on a hurt friend who has none",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.loop2.why"] = "it covers steady damage",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.loop3.if"] = "on whoever is hurt worst",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.loop3.why"] = "it is your efficient heal",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.loop4.if"] = "until you learn Heal at 16",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.loop4.why"] = "it is the heal you have before then",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.loop5.why"] = "the wand adds damage and costs no mana",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.name"] = "In a group",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.opening1.if"] = "on each party member",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.opening1.why"] = "more health for everyone",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.opening2.if"] = "on yourself, before the pull",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.opening2.why"] = "damage then cannot stop your heals",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.opening3.if"] = "on the tank, before the pull",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.opening3.why"] = "it heals over time while you aim the next heal",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.alt.say"] = "when you heal a party instead of fighting",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.between1.if"] = "after a fight, if you are hurt",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.between1.why"] = "it heals while you drink",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.between2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.between2.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.priest-discipline.s2.between2.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
