  ["forever.warlock-affliction.split"] = "the last points and the demon. Mobalytics' Crix, the newest, leaves Siphon Life and Wrack for the end. Kargoz and Icy Veins take Siphon Life at 30, and Wrack when it opens at 40. Kargoz also respecs at 22 into a build that drains. The order here is Crix's.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.dry"] = "A demon that dies ends your Soul Link, so keep it alive.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.intro"] = "Demonology turns your demon into the other half of your damage, and Soul Link shares what hits you with it. It is the sturdy way to play a Warlock, with fewer spells to juggle.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.line"] = "A strong demon, Searing Pain to mark the monster, Soul Link to share the hits. The sturdy way to level.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.note"] = "(31 points in Demonology, then 20 in Affliction for instant Corruption and the drain.)",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p1"] = "Corruption casts faster, and you start using it now. More ranks come later and make it instant.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p10"] = "A share of the damage you take goes to your demon, and you both hit harder. It is why the build is sturdy, so keep the demon alive.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p11"] = "You and your demon gain spell damage that grows with your level while a demon is out. Keep one out at all times.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p12"] = "More health and mana for your demon, and more mana for you. It is a spare point that opens the way to Master Demonologist.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p13"] = "You and the demon you have out gain a bonus that depends on which demon it is. Read which one yours gives before you swap.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p14"] = "Your Demonic Sacrifice stays on when you summon a different demon. Sacrifice the Imp, then use the Voidwalker or the Succubus.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p15"] = "Corruption is now instant, so you cast it as you walk and put it on a second monster.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p16"] = "Your Affliction spells reach further, so you open from farther away while your demon runs in.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p17"] = "Fewer missed spells and less threat on you. A miss is mana spent for nothing.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p18"] = "A hit mostly no longer pushes back your Drain Life, so the drain works when a monster reaches you.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p19"] = "Your next Bane of Agony or Curse of Weakness is stronger, and so is your next Curse of Exhaustion. Cast it just before the Bane.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p2"] = "Every demon you have hits harder. In this build the demon does much of the killing, so it comes first.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p20"] = "Bane of Agony hurts a little more. You cast it on every monster, so a small rise adds up.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p21"] = "A slow for a monster that is running off, or one you are running from. Only one Curse per Warlock can be on a monster.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p22"] = "Corruption and Drain Life ticks can make your next Shadow Bolt instant. Spend it at once.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p23"] = "Bane of Agony hurts a little more. You cast it on every monster, so a small rise adds up.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p24"] = "The last point is a free choice. A fourth rank of Suppression means fewer misses and less threat on you.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p3"] = "Your demon heals from the damage you deal and gets mana back when you Life Tap. It tanks for longer without you stopping to heal it.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p4"] = "The Voidwalker's taunt, shield and heal work better. It is the demon that holds one monster while you work on another.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p5"] = "Summoning a demon is faster and costs less mana. Swapping demons for the job is part of this build, so it should not cost a pull.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p6"] = "Succubus and Incubus hit and charm better. Worth it when the Succubus is your demon for single monsters.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p7"] = "Searing Pain marks a monster, and your demon's next three hits on it hurt more. Mark whatever your demon is fighting.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p8"] = "Your next summon is much faster and costs half the mana. Use it to swap demons in the middle of a fight.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.p9"] = "Gives up your demon for a bonus that lasts. You will not use it until Demonic Pact lets you keep the bonus and call another demon.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.s1"] = "Before your first talent point. The same kit in every build.",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.s1.between1.if"] = "after a fight, if your health is high",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.s1.between1.why"] = "it turns spare health into the mana you need",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.s1.between2.if"] = "after a fight, before the next pull",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.s1.between2.text"] = "Sit and drink",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.s1.between2.why"] = "mana from drinking is cheap, and a pull on empty is not",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.s1.loop1.if"] = "on a monster that will live a while",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.s1.loop1.why"] = "it hurts most at the end, so cast it early",
  ["forever.warlock-demonology.s1.loop2.if"] = "when it is not on the monster",
